│   ├── domain/
│   │   ├── contracts.js
│   │   ├── ScoreEntry.js
│   │   └── validation.js
│   ├── games/
│   │   └── FlappyBird.js
│   ├── infrastructure/
│   │   ├── FirebaseLeaderboard.js
│   │   └── LocalLeaderboard.js
│   └── presentation/
│       └── app.js
```

`LocalLeaderboard.js` is at `src/infrastructure/LocalLeaderboard.js`
`contracts.js` is at `src/domain/contracts.js`

Relative path from `src/infrastructure/` to `src/domain/` = `../domain/`
So `../domain/contracts.js` ✓
But `../../domain/contracts.js` = goes up two levels from `src/infrastructure/` to root, then `domain/contracts.js` = `domain/contracts.js` which doesn't exist ❌

This will cause a 404 when the browser tries to load the module. That's the main issue.

But the user said "нихуя ничего не работает" - let me think if there could be more issues...

Actually, there's another subtle issue. In `app.js`:
```js
game.mount(canvas);
game.start();
```

But `FlappyBird.js` `mount` function is:
```js
function mount(canvasEl, input, loop) {
    window.addEventListener('keydown', onKeyDown);
}
```

It ignores the canvas param and uses the one from closure. That's fine.

But `start()` calls `loop()` which calls `draw()`. The canvas was already used to get `ctx` in the closure. So drawing should work.

Let me also think about `game.mount(canvas)` — wait, actually `game.mount(canvas)` is called each time `startGame()` runs AND each time restart happens. In restart, `dispose()` removes the listener and clears callbacks, then `mount()` adds the listener back. But `dispose()` also sets `running = false`, which is important.

Let me look at `start()` more carefully:
```js
function start() {
    reset();
    running = true;
    paused = false;
    if (frameId) cancelAnimationFrame(frameId);
    loop();  // direct call, not RAF
}
```

`loop()`:
```js
function loop() {
    if (!running || paused) return;
    ...
    draw();
    frameId = requestAnimationFrame(loop);
}
```

First frame is synchronously executed, which is fine. Then RAF continues.

OK, I think the main bug is the import path in `LocalLeaderboard.js`. Let me fix it.

